8 Applications And Integrations
*******************************

Emacsvox prepares speech support for many Emacs modes as their libraries
are loaded.  Start the application normally; when its buffer appears,
use ‘C-h m’ for the active modes and their commands, ‘C-h b’ for the
effective bindings, and ‘C-h k’ followed by a key to identify one
binding.  The generated *note (emacsvox-reference)Emacsvox Commands And
Options:: records the public Emacsvox commands and options.

   This chapter is a curated starting point, not a promise that every
module in the generated reference has a maintained task guide.  Emacs
itself or a third-party package provides the application's general
operation; Emacsvox adds the speech feedback.  Consult both sets of help
when diagnosing a problem.

   Earlier Emacspeak surveys, including their W3, Dismal, and
scanner/OCR setup, are preserved as historical material in *note
Historical Application Survey: (emacsvox-heritage)Emacs Packages.  They
are not current setup instructions.

