8.6 Editing Code
================

Programming modes provide language-aware movement, indentation,
compilation, and navigation.  Emacsvox speaks those operations and uses
voice-lock to distinguish faces such as comments, strings, warnings, and
language constructs.  Use ‘C-h m’ in the source buffer for the language
mode, and search the generated reference for an integration named after
that mode.


File: emacsvox.info,  Node: Development Environment,  Next: Desktop Management,  Prev: Editing Code,  Up: Emacs Packages

8.7 Development Environment
===========================

Emacs can combine compilation, diagnostics, project navigation, version
control, debuggers, and language servers into a development environment.
Emacsvox supplies speech feedback to many of those components, but their
own manuals remain authoritative for setup and operation.  Verify each
component individually with its mode help before combining it into a
larger workflow.


